WEBVTT

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:10.800
Sara Werec...

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:14.030
That was once my name,
but I am no longer her.

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:20.650
Sara Cruz, Mobile Troops cadet at
Basion Tactical Training School.

00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:23.180
That is who I am now.

00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:26.380
Team #6, intercept TUMORs at T-653!

00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:28.190
601. Roger!

00:00:28.190 --> 00:00:29.490
602. Roger!

00:00:29.490 --> 00:00:30.960
603. Roger!

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:32.220
604. Roger!

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:33.950
605. Roger!

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:43.000
606! Cadet Sara Cruz!

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:45.040
606. Roger!

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:47.740
Quit your daydreaming, newbie!

00:00:47.740 --> 00:00:50.670
Strain contact! Commence exercise!

00:00:53.570 --> 00:00:57.990
Encounter

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:04.150
Exercise duration: 23 minutes.
No damage to Strains or Gambees.

00:01:04.150 --> 00:01:05.920
Headmaster Craven.

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:09.450
We've had another successful
interdivisional exercise.

00:01:09.450 --> 00:01:12.910
Yes. Both divisions are doing very well.

00:01:13.990 --> 00:01:14.960
Sir?

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:17.730
It seems someone's
a bit off on their own...

00:01:17.730 --> 00:01:20.630
Jake-kun. Who is that?

00:01:20.630 --> 00:01:26.300
Oh. Gambee 606, Sara Cruz.
She transferred here three months ago.

00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:29.240
She's a bit behind in terms of skill.

00:01:29.240 --> 00:01:34.440
I see. She's doing
quite well, nonetheless.

00:01:56.070 --> 00:01:59.240
I could take these down
so easily in a Strain.

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:01.410
But that's not possible now.

00:02:01.410 --> 00:02:05.870
I lost my Mimic...
my ability to pilot a Strain.

00:02:07.550 --> 00:02:13.050
I lost everything on that day,
with my brother's betrayal.

00:02:13.050 --> 00:02:16.220
And all that remained were questions.

00:02:16.220 --> 00:02:20.160
Why did my gentle brother do what he did?

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:23.330
What changed him?

00:02:23.330 --> 00:02:27.600
What things had those cold eyes seen?

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:30.900
Exercise complete.
All units, return to ship.

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:35.140
To find out the truth,
I'll need to see my brother again.

00:02:35.140 --> 00:02:38.740
And the only way to do that
is to go to the front lines.

00:02:38.740 --> 00:02:40.610
That's why I'm here.

00:02:59.500 --> 00:03:01.630
Sara Cruz!

00:03:01.630 --> 00:03:04.370
Do you even understand
the concept of teamwork?!

00:03:04.370 --> 00:03:06.540
I've looked the other way
since you're new,

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:08.170
but what was that today?!

00:03:08.170 --> 00:03:10.880
Do you think you can wipe out
TUMORs all by yourself?!

00:03:10.880 --> 00:03:13.850
Especially when you suck
at Gambee piloting?

00:03:13.850 --> 00:03:17.420
Or are you trying to stand out
so you can earn some points?

00:03:17.420 --> 00:03:19.020
No.

00:03:19.020 --> 00:03:23.290
I went off on my own because
the rest of you choose easy targets.

00:03:23.290 --> 00:03:26.620
That's not a very realistic
"actual combat scenario."

00:03:28.030 --> 00:03:30.160
S-say what?!

00:03:30.160 --> 00:03:33.630
It's basic knowledge that TUMORs
come in groups in real combat.

00:03:33.630 --> 00:03:36.940
Taking them on your way
would be pointless.

00:03:36.940 --> 00:03:38.770
--Why, you...
--Isabella!

00:03:38.770 --> 00:03:40.970
What, Mariette?!

00:03:42.810 --> 00:03:44.910
Lottie Gelh from the
Spatial Armor Division!

00:03:44.910 --> 00:03:49.380
That's enough, now!
Intimidating newcomers is disgraceful!

00:03:49.380 --> 00:03:52.220
Please stay out of the
Mobile Troops Division's business!

00:03:52.220 --> 00:03:53.490
My apologies.

00:03:53.490 --> 00:03:55.820
It's just that her argument
was more sound than yours,

00:03:55.820 --> 00:03:57.560
so I was a tad curious.

00:03:57.560 --> 00:03:59.990
Though, it is hard to believe
the famous Gambee pilot

00:03:59.990 --> 00:04:02.390
known as the Lioness
would choose her targets.

00:04:02.390 --> 00:04:07.020
Or else we wouldn't be able to rest
easy with you protecting the ship.

00:04:10.340 --> 00:04:13.940
Lottie... You shouldn't get so involved.

00:04:13.940 --> 00:04:16.370
I can't stand people like that, you see.

00:04:16.370 --> 00:04:21.470
But she seems to fight
the way a Reasoner would.

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:44.270
--She's so uncute, as always!
--She's so gloomy...

00:04:44.270 --> 00:04:45.930
Talk about creepy!

00:04:49.670 --> 00:04:53.140
Only you can accomplish
what you've decided.

00:04:53.140 --> 00:04:57.140
As long as you believe in that,
there's surely nothing you can't do!

00:05:11.130 --> 00:05:14.770
Hear you had a spat with the "Queen"
of Spatial Armor yesterday.

00:05:14.770 --> 00:05:15.530
Yeah.

00:05:15.530 --> 00:05:20.440
What an annoying tramp! All I did
was give a newbie some advice.

00:05:20.440 --> 00:05:21.970
Newbie? You mean "her"?

00:05:21.970 --> 00:05:24.310
Yeah. That smartass girl.

00:05:24.310 --> 00:05:28.280
I dunno where she came from,
but there's nothing good about her.

00:05:28.280 --> 00:05:32.020
Think she'll be coming with us
for the sub-light speed exercises?

00:05:32.020 --> 00:05:35.020
That reminds me, she was
arguing with Jake the other day

00:05:35.020 --> 00:05:36.420
about catching up to regulation standards.

00:05:36.420 --> 00:05:40.330
She just transferred here!
She'll never make it in time!

00:05:40.330 --> 00:05:43.820
Or maybe she'll bat her eyelashes
at the instructors or something!

00:05:46.260 --> 00:05:47.770
Forget it! Forget it!

00:05:47.770 --> 00:05:51.200
I've told you time and time again,
I can't OK this schedule!

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:53.100
But...

00:05:53.100 --> 00:05:57.780
Why are you in such a rush?!
Tell me why you're in such a hurry!

00:05:57.780 --> 00:05:59.440
It's...

00:06:03.550 --> 00:06:05.550
Four weeks.

00:06:05.550 --> 00:06:09.020
Pass the Basion descent
exercise four weeks from now.

00:06:09.020 --> 00:06:12.350
Do that, and I'll consider you
for the sub-light speed exercises.

00:06:15.830 --> 00:06:17.530
Think she'll be able to do it?

00:06:17.530 --> 00:06:23.400
Probably not. But even then,
I doubt she'll give up.

00:06:31.810 --> 00:06:33.300
The thrusters!

00:07:02.810 --> 00:07:07.540
This is a TUMOR, a Deague insect.
As you can see, it's...

00:07:17.860 --> 00:07:19.020
Alright!

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:28.030
That was...

00:07:28.030 --> 00:07:29.200
Huh?

00:07:29.200 --> 00:07:31.800
The Gambee pilot from the other day!

00:07:31.800 --> 00:07:33.770
--Jessie! Let's go!
--Eh?!

00:07:37.440 --> 00:07:40.380
Increasing to specified gravity.

00:07:47.690 --> 00:07:52.490
Oh! Four Gs, huh?
I think I'll do the same!

00:07:52.490 --> 00:07:54.960
Increasing to specified gravity.

00:08:02.800 --> 00:08:04.500
Why do I have to do this?

00:08:04.500 --> 00:08:09.840
Word is there's this Gambee pilot
who's really pushing herself hard!

00:08:11.510 --> 00:08:13.140
Why are you in such a hurry?

00:08:13.140 --> 00:08:15.680
It's none of your business.

00:08:15.680 --> 00:08:17.770
That's true!

00:08:21.290 --> 00:08:25.280
What do you say to a contest?
To see who gets tired out first...

00:08:42.940 --> 00:08:44.710
It's her!

00:08:44.710 --> 00:08:47.750
Let's save it for later, Isabella.

00:08:47.750 --> 00:08:51.450
Lottie Gelh? Why are they together?!

00:08:51.450 --> 00:08:56.250
I get it! Thinks she can mock me...

00:08:56.250 --> 00:08:57.410
Isabella?!

00:09:08.470 --> 00:09:10.670
Y-you should really stop now...

00:09:10.670 --> 00:09:13.000
This is crazy!

00:09:13.000 --> 00:09:17.140
I- I know that! But she's-

00:09:17.140 --> 00:09:22.480
If you can't keep up, then stop.
This is my daily routine.

00:09:22.480 --> 00:09:24.470
There you have it!

00:09:50.380 --> 00:09:53.040
I figured this would happen...

00:10:01.390 --> 00:10:04.090
She's got real guts!

00:10:04.090 --> 00:10:07.750
Hey. You ever heard of
"all things in moderation"?

00:10:14.100 --> 00:10:16.190
How're you feeling?

00:10:17.470 --> 00:10:19.440
Whoa, now. Stay in bed!

00:10:19.440 --> 00:10:20.270
But...

00:10:20.270 --> 00:10:23.070
You still have an hour
until your IV is done.

00:10:23.070 --> 00:10:25.410
Just take it easy until then.

00:10:25.410 --> 00:10:28.980
Looks like you're not the only
one who goes too far, Queen.

00:10:28.980 --> 00:10:31.350
B-be quiet!

00:10:31.350 --> 00:10:35.090
Faculty member Ben Trafetta Hughes,
please come to the bridge.

00:10:35.090 --> 00:10:38.080
Listen, now. Stay in bed!

00:10:41.760 --> 00:10:44.750
I never thought you'd go that far.

00:10:46.560 --> 00:10:49.120
--I'm Lottie Gelh. How about you?

00:10:47.770 --> 00:10:51.120
--It is now 6:00 p.m. Basion Standard Time.

00:10:49.130 --> 00:10:51.580
--Sara. Sara Wer-

00:10:51.140 --> 00:10:53.450
--Here is the news.

00:10:52.570 --> 00:10:54.160
--Sara Cruz...

00:10:53.440 --> 00:10:55.960
--First, we bring you new information

00:10:54.170 --> 00:10:57.630
--Sara, huh? It's nice to meet you!

00:10:55.970 --> 00:11:01.110
--regarding the 7008 O.E. attack on Grabera.

00:11:01.110 --> 00:11:03.250
Video from the scene of Ralph Werec,

00:11:03.250 --> 00:11:07.290
the suspected Deague defector,
has been made public.

00:11:07.290 --> 00:11:10.090
This video was recovered from
the data of a surveillance camera

00:11:10.090 --> 00:11:12.490
left inside the military
research facility.

00:11:12.490 --> 00:11:17.160
It appears that he led
the well-planned attack,

00:11:17.160 --> 00:11:21.230
but it is unknown why the current
head of the Werec family

00:11:21.230 --> 00:11:24.240
--Ralph... Werec...
--which has produced outstanding
Reasoners for centuries now,

00:11:24.240 --> 00:11:25.930
has suddenly joined
forces with the Deague.

00:11:29.140 --> 00:11:31.140
We will now begin your descent exercise

00:11:31.140 --> 00:11:33.880
into the gas clouds of Planet Basion.

00:11:33.880 --> 00:11:38.220
Once this is over, only your
sub-light speed exercises will remain.

00:11:38.220 --> 00:11:40.820
For those who still aren't up to regulation,
this is your last chance!

00:11:40.820 --> 00:11:42.590
Good luck!

00:11:42.590 --> 00:11:44.720
The objective is very simple.

00:11:44.720 --> 00:11:49.090
Retrieve a float suspended inside
the gas clouds and return to ship!

00:11:51.560 --> 00:11:55.170
Only you can accomplish
what you've decided.

00:11:55.170 --> 00:11:58.970
As long as you believe in that,
there's surely nothing you can't do.

00:11:58.970 --> 00:12:01.670
There's surely nothing... I can't do!

00:12:06.780 --> 00:12:09.610
No one has passed this exercise
in the past six terms.

00:12:09.610 --> 00:12:12.920
The harshness of this planet's
environment is the reason.

00:12:12.920 --> 00:12:13.920
As you know,

00:12:13.920 --> 00:12:16.850
powerful electromagnetic storms
sweep through the gas clouds

00:12:16.850 --> 00:12:20.430
and can greatly impair your unit's
electronics and capabilities.

00:12:20.430 --> 00:12:23.390
Naturally, radar and such will be useless.

00:12:23.390 --> 00:12:26.730
All you have to rely on are
your own skills and instinct!

00:12:36.710 --> 00:12:38.980
There we go...

00:12:38.980 --> 00:12:41.310
Hey! Hand it here!

00:12:46.520 --> 00:12:47.690
Honestly, now!

00:12:47.690 --> 00:12:51.190
I told you! It doesn't
understand when you're so vague!

00:12:51.190 --> 00:12:53.090
Shut up, Carmichael!

00:12:53.090 --> 00:12:57.860
A.I. learns from repeated mistakes!
So this is fine!

00:12:57.860 --> 00:12:59.260
Hey! That!

00:13:00.260 --> 00:13:03.030
You're the one who's learning, Melchi...

00:13:05.600 --> 00:13:08.970
Is our Engineering Division going
to be okay with teachers like this?

00:13:08.970 --> 00:13:10.480
Leave me alone.

00:13:10.480 --> 00:13:15.850
So? What does the Queen Reasoner
want in a place like this?

00:13:15.850 --> 00:13:17.640
I have a small favor to ask...

00:13:22.990 --> 00:13:25.290
The coordinates are right
around here, but...

00:13:28.890 --> 00:13:30.730
Found ya!

00:13:30.730 --> 00:13:32.660
--This the one?
--Yup!

00:13:32.660 --> 00:13:35.470
Say, why do you want to watch this?

00:13:35.470 --> 00:13:37.800
I'm just a little curious about her...

00:13:46.480 --> 00:13:47.810
There it is!

00:13:50.820 --> 00:13:51.520
What?!

00:13:51.520 --> 00:13:54.540
I refuse to let you have it, Sara!

00:13:58.620 --> 00:14:00.960
Isabella! Why?!

00:14:00.960 --> 00:14:02.090
Isn't it obvious?

00:14:02.090 --> 00:14:05.960
Because I hate you!
Because I don't want you to win!

00:14:05.960 --> 00:14:09.200
Because I can't lose to someone
who sucks up to Reasoners

00:14:09.200 --> 00:14:11.700
and mocks other people!

00:14:11.700 --> 00:14:14.710
Oh, my! What a weird one!

00:14:14.710 --> 00:14:17.230
Must be that idiot.

00:14:19.310 --> 00:14:21.310
It's mine!

00:14:21.310 --> 00:14:23.110
What?!

00:14:23.110 --> 00:14:24.310
Isabella!

00:14:29.320 --> 00:14:33.560
She just had to be reckless.
Now she's going to enter a crash orbit...

00:14:33.560 --> 00:14:35.230
The unit isn't damaged much,

00:14:35.230 --> 00:14:37.460
but the person inside seems
to be unconscious.

00:14:37.460 --> 00:14:41.600
Can't we do something from our end?
Remote control or something?

00:14:41.600 --> 00:14:43.900
The gas clouds would make it impossible.

00:14:43.900 --> 00:14:46.600
I'm not even sure if Jake and the others
are aware of the situation...

00:14:46.600 --> 00:14:48.170
Eh?! Then...

00:14:48.170 --> 00:14:49.470
Yeah...

00:15:08.090 --> 00:15:10.960
Well done, Cadet Cruz!

00:15:10.960 --> 00:15:13.660
To think you'd be the first person
to pass in six school terms!

00:15:13.660 --> 00:15:17.130
As promised, I will let you join
the sub-light speed exercises!

00:15:17.130 --> 00:15:20.640
--Is that acceptable, Headmaster?
--Yes, of course!

00:15:20.640 --> 00:15:25.200
It is our duty to promote more and more
top-rate personnel, after all.

00:15:26.710 --> 00:15:29.280
Sara Cruz! You little...

00:15:29.280 --> 00:15:31.280
What were you thinking, shooting an ally?!

00:15:31.280 --> 00:15:32.850
Are you trying to kill me?!

00:15:32.850 --> 00:15:36.020
Is that how badly you wanted to beat me?!

00:15:36.020 --> 00:15:38.350
Say something, dammit!

00:15:39.860 --> 00:15:41.020
Hold it!

00:15:44.760 --> 00:15:46.900
I'm going to report this to the instructor!

00:15:46.900 --> 00:15:48.470
Are you sure?

00:15:48.470 --> 00:15:51.600
If you do that, you're the ones
who'll be shamed, you know.

00:15:51.600 --> 00:15:52.740
What?!

00:15:52.740 --> 00:15:56.610
A pilot who stupidly crashes
into a rock and passes out

00:15:56.610 --> 00:15:58.940
and a unit that's out of control...

00:15:58.940 --> 00:16:02.610
What would be the quickest
way to save them?

00:16:14.830 --> 00:16:16.690
W-what?!

00:16:25.970 --> 00:16:28.300
...Or something along those lines, right?

00:16:30.980 --> 00:16:33.310
--Isabella?!
--Wait! Hold on!

00:16:37.350 --> 00:16:39.680
Why didn't you argue back?

00:17:12.520 --> 00:17:13.850
No!

00:17:22.030 --> 00:17:24.790
Where is it?! Where is it?!
My pendant!

00:17:27.260 --> 00:17:29.930
Where?! Where is it?!

00:17:31.200 --> 00:17:33.860
Where?! Where did it go?!

00:17:42.250 --> 00:17:45.820
Hey! That's enough!
We gotta do our work now!

00:17:45.820 --> 00:17:48.390
Shut up! Leave me alone!

00:17:48.390 --> 00:17:49.880
Why, you...

00:18:48.650 --> 00:18:52.170
This is... a Strain?

00:19:01.390 --> 00:19:07.420
What are you doing here
in such a dark place, all alone?

00:19:09.030 --> 00:19:12.590
You're so dirty... You poor thing...

00:19:15.740 --> 00:19:17.680
This is...

00:19:17.680 --> 00:19:19.340
...a Mimic!

00:19:20.510 --> 00:19:22.740
"Emily..."

00:19:25.820 --> 00:19:31.490
Oh, I see. You don't have a Reasoner...

00:19:31.490 --> 00:19:35.150
It must be lonely, all by yourself...

00:19:37.630 --> 00:19:43.700
Actually, I lost things dear to me, too...

00:19:43.700 --> 00:19:48.370
I lost them... I lost them all...

00:19:54.550 --> 00:19:59.350
I guess we're in the same
situation, Emily...

00:20:15.400 --> 00:20:17.000
"Emily..."

00:20:17.000 --> 00:20:19.130
My name...

00:20:30.780 --> 00:20:33.680
Unchanging daily routine.
Days of unpleasantness.

00:20:33.680 --> 00:20:37.120
A miracle occurs in the unusual
situation of sub-light speed combat.

00:20:37.120 --> 00:20:40.820
On the next Soukou no Strain:
Sub-Light Speed Nightmare

00:20:40.820 --> 00:20:42.810
My brother is here!
